### Page 2 of 2

```text
(iii)
The area sought to be annexed is a logical and feasible addition to the
annexing city or town and the extension of basic and other services
customarily available to residents ofthe city or town shall, within reason, be
available to the area proposed to be annexed;
(iv)
The area sought to be annexed is contiguous with or adjacent to the annexing
city or town, or the area meets the requirements of W.S. § 15-1-407;
(v)
If the city or town does not own or operate its own electric utility, its
governing body is prepared to issue one (1) or more franchises as necessary
to serve the annexed area pursuant to W.S. § 15-1-410; and
(vi)
The annexing city or town, not less than twenty (20) business days prior to
the public hearing required by W.S. § 15-1-405(a), will send by certified mail
to all landowners and affected public utilities within the territory a summary
of the annexation report as required under subsection (c) of this section and
notice of the time, date and location of the public hearing required by W.S.
§ 15-1-405(a).
WHEREAS, an annexation report has been created by the annexing City, containing,
at a minimum, the required information from W.S. § 15-1-402(c). The City of Cheyenne
shall prepare for each landowner and affected public utility so requesting in writing, the
estimated cost ofinfrastructure improvements required ofthe landowner and affected public
utility related to the annexation pursuant to W.S. § 15-1-402(e); and
WHEREAS, the annexation of this land does not create an area which is situated
entirely within the boundaries of the City but is not annexed; and
WHEREAS, this land does not meet the criteria under W.S. § 15-1-412 requiring
an owner’s signature for annexation.
NOW, THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, THAT the land described above is compliant
withW.S. § 15-1-402,andthattheproceduresoutlinedinW.S. § 15-1-405 and W.S. § 15-1-
406 shall hereby be initiated.
PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED THIS
DAY OF DECEMBER,
2019.
MARIAN J. ORR, MAYOR
